%% M2 integration design: which integration patterns pricing-service uses, and why.
%% Honest scope note: M2 publishes NO Kafka events. Pricing is a synchronous
%% question-and-answer service, so request/reply is the only messaging style it needs;
%% publish/subscribe and the broker belong to the parcel and notification flows (M3/M4).
flowchart LR
    classDef rr fill:#eef4ff,stroke:#3b5bdb,color:#1b2a5e
    classDef cache fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#e8590c,color:#7f2d00
    classDef gate fill:#f3f0ff,stroke:#7048e8,color:#3c2a85
    classDef none fill:#f8f9fa,stroke:#adb5bd,stroke-dasharray:5 4,color:#868e96

    BROWSER["Browser<br/>fee-estimate widget"]:::rr
    BFF["Next.js BFF<br/>token stays server-side"]:::gate
    GW["api-gateway<br/>single choke point"]:::gate
    PS["pricing-service"]:::rr
    PARCEL["parcel-service (M3)"]:::rr
    PG[("Postgres pricing_db")]:::rr
    RD[("Redis<br/>quote snapshot")]:::cache
    KAFKA["Kafka broker<br/>(publish/subscribe)"]:::none

    BROWSER -->|"1. Request/Reply (sync REST)<br/>POST /pricing/quotes - the user needs the fee now"| BFF
    BFF -->|"2. API Gateway / BFF<br/>facade: one entry point, no token in browser JS"| GW
    GW -->|"3. Request/Reply<br/>routed to /api/v1/pricing/**"| PS
    PS -->|"4. Repository over JDBC<br/>reference data: zones, districts, rate cards, size classes"| PG
    PS -->|"5. Cache-aside write / handoff token<br/>SET quoteId -> snapshot, EX 900"| RD
    PARCEL -->|"6. Request/Reply<br/>GET /pricing/quotes/{id} before accepting a booking"| GW
    PS -.->|"7. NOT used by M2<br/>no pricing event is published"| KAFKA
